$F(\bar{k})$-torsor) by $\sigma \cdot a = c(\sigma)\cdot \sigma(a)$; this is
compatible with the $F(\bar{k})$-action, and the equivalence of categories
produces an $F_X$-torsor on $X_{\mathrm{et}}$.


